  "body": "What happens:\nThe toolbar icons for Rotary Contour and Rotary Parallel look very similar at 16px size. Both show a cylinder with a tool on the right, and the internal line pattern (vertical vs horizontal) is hard to distinguish at small size. The operations have fundamentally different axis orientations:\n\n- Rotary Contour: part axis = Z (standing up, lathe), waterline rings around axis\n- Rotary Parallel: part axis = X (laid down, mill with A/B), generatrix passes along axis\n\nExpected:\nIcons that clearly communicate the axis orientation difference at a glance. Possible approaches:\n- Show the axis direction (Z arrow for Contour, X arrow for Parallel)\n- Show the part orientation (standing cylinder vs lying cylinder)\n- Use distinct visual metaphors (rings vs straight passes)\n\nEvidence:\nIcons are in assets/ui/svg/op-rotary-contour.svg and op-rotary-parallel.svg. Both rendered at 16px in toolbar.\n\nDone means:\n- New SVG icons for Rotary Contour and Rotary Parallel that are visually distinct at 16px\n- Each icon clearly shows the part's axis orientation (Z vs X)\n- Updated PNGs generated from SVGs (32x32, drawn at 16px)\n- No regression in toolbar layout or icon references",
